{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact candidate f75ca1f8071cba659cd5ac041071fd3c36b5ca8a, all 12 artifacts inspected and bound to that head. Reporting artifact packages/room/README.md@f75ca1f8071cba659cd5ac041071fd3c36b5ca8a, Request c657d4ba. This answers clock finding git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b3445eae059394ed3143293792021480272a644a; the replaced 26dbb298 invitation is not the basis of this verdict.\n\nArchitecture: affected layers are Room admission and redemption, HTTPS/RPC transport, the typed client, and the protocol. Same-head docs/protocol.md section 31 reconciles R-ADM-8 with R-GEN-6/R-SEC-4 and specifies R-CRED-9 replay and bounded limiter behaviour. This repository has no docs/reference/architecture.md; the protocol and Room README carry its affected contracts. submit preserves its public result shape while internal admit reports whether this call admitted or replayed. A repeated redemption issues no session; key possession recovers the original join record and a separately signed session. recoverJoin now receives ClientOptions.now, defaults to Date.now, and reads the clock inside each retry. It reuses the original join bytes and idempotency key and makes a fresh signed session request at the current injected time. The old defective supplied-clock case now passes against the actual Room, including the retained checker fixture.\n\nSecurity: a public logged join cannot obtain a session through redemption replay; concurrent identical redemptions issue one session. Refused joins on HTTP and RPC leave neither log nor idempotency record containing a still-live invitation secret, while other recordable refusals remain recorded. Per-invitation limits cover joins on submit and both redemption paths, count only issued invitation IDs, expire windows and cap each Room's table at 10,000. HTTPS address limits remain; service-binding callers share no invented address. Outer input shape is checked before address limiting, and join admission still performs its shape, signature and authority checks. The fresh-session recovery proves possession of the joining key; changing its clock does not weaken those checks or the 300-second window. The original three repairs' security conclusions from 812fb907 remain supported at this head.\n\nSimplification: the internal result discriminator and small per-Room limiter avoid duplicating admission or retaining arbitrary caller keys. The clock is one injected helper argument, with the existing public default preserved. No extra protocol type, public caller obligation, persistent limiter or scope reduction is needed. The README merge retains both reports. Its historical 411-test paragraph describes the clock-only head; the invitation reports 418 Room workerd tests at this merge, independently confirmed below.\n\nIndependent evidence: clean exact-head npm ci and root npm run typecheck exit 0; root npm test exit 0 with 2,094 passed and 1 skipped, including Room Node 138/DO 418, client Node 88/DO 2 and CLI 162. In a separate exact-head diagnostic checkout with its own workspace dependency links, I reran 13 non-equivalent original guard mutations plus 3 clock mutations: all 16 produce named runtime assertion failures, with no compile or import failures. Removing the clock or replacing it with Date.now fails the actual Room supplied-clock and moved-clock tests; reading it once outside retries fails the actual Room ten-minute clock-move test. The redundant malformed-ID string check is not counted as a killed mutation. After restoring every source file, the Room targeted controls pass 17/17 and client redemption controls pass 17/17, and tracked status is clean in both checkouts. No live deployment, provider operation or real credential use. git diff --check has two nonblocking trailing blank lines, in docs/protocol.md:3277 and request-c657d4ba.test.ts:301.\n\nIntegration: f75ca1f8 incorporates approved main hygiene 7cf6aae025c192e2d2a5e38e72e745773a46d2cd and plan 003. I read the remerge diff: only README report placement was manually resolved, both sections remain, and the worker/Room source changes over main are the intended nullable service address. The combined root gates pass. This approval establishes this exact candidate, not live deployment or whole-platform Jam/self-host readiness.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9f99ac6dcc727d40a80f11b4a50766c9c4037be5","binding":"assigned","head":"f75ca1f8071cba659cd5ac041071fd3c36b5ca8a","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8feeb8da040c49141356affe446738ca4e91b4ed\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:86123511453e26cb3a649a617af5e1051c968591\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4588f0668e697648b4c4154442e0219f2e85fc96","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}